1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:12,233
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,967 --> 00:00:33,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,267 --> 00:00:35,300
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:41,400
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,367 --> 00:00:44,067
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,167 --> 00:00:45,133
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:46,333
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:51,500
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:54,100
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:55,667
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,933 --> 00:00:58,133
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,267 --> 00:01:00,633
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,167 --> 00:01:03,467
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:06,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:12,133
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,233 --> 00:01:13,100
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:14,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,033 --> 00:01:22,267
<i>All the gold, all the jewelry,
and records.</i>

21
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:23,600
<i> We need to squeeze the Zafras.</i>

22
00:01:23,733 --> 00:01:25,933
<i> He is using his influence</i>

23
00:01:26,067 --> 00:01:30,033
<i>to take down all
of our businesses one by one!</i>

24
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:31,800
<i>It's an empty shell.
We have to check if it's similar</i>

25
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:34,100
<i>to the empty shell we saw
on Soriano Street.</i>

26
00:01:34,233 --> 00:01:35,267
<i> What are you waiting for?</i>

27
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:37,600
<i>Go get changed so we can keep
the party going!</i>

28
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:40,533
<i>Love, I also bought you
other clothes.</i>

29
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,200
<i> Thank you. This is beautiful!</i>

30
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,567
<i>- Time to drink!
- [CHANTING] Tekla! Tekla!</i>

31
00:01:46,667 --> 00:01:49,800
- [POLICE SIRENS BLARING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

32
00:01:49,933 --> 00:01:51,233
[GUARD]
Sir, what's all this commotion?

33
00:01:51,367 --> 00:01:53,067
We have a warrant
to search this place.

34
00:01:53,233 --> 00:01:55,233
Sir,
our business operates legally!

35
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,167
That's what we want
to find out.

36
00:01:57,267 --> 00:01:58,700
Based on our intel...

37
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:03,567
Your gold came from
an illegal mining operation.

38
00:02:03,733 --> 00:02:05,367
So stop giving us
a hard time, okay?

39
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,033
- Santos!
- Hey. Open the gate!

40
00:02:08,167 --> 00:02:09,533
[GATE CLANGING]

41
00:02:09,667 --> 00:02:12,067
This is a raid! Get down!
Put your hands up!

42
00:02:12,233 --> 00:02:14,867
- Put your hands up!
- Bring everyone to the center!

43
00:02:15,033 --> 00:02:16,033
Walk to the center!

44
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:17,267
[BOX LID THUDS]

45
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,667
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [POLICE SHOUTING]

46
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:23,100
[GUNSHOTS]

47
00:02:23,267 --> 00:02:24,200
Clear the area!

48
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:27,567
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:28,700
Clear!

50
00:02:31,633 --> 00:02:33,700
- Sir.
- Bring these in for evidence.

51
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,900
[BOX LID THUDS]

52
00:02:36,033 --> 00:02:40,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,867
Hey. Bring all of these
to the station.

54
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:44,000
Yes, sir.

55
00:02:44,133 --> 00:02:46,067
Santos! Follow me.

56
00:02:48,567 --> 00:02:50,933
[DOOR THUDS]

57
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,967
[UMALI CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

58
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:01,067
[POLICE] Stand! Stand!
Stand! Stand!

59
00:03:02,167 --> 00:03:03,100
Hurry up!

60
00:03:05,333 --> 00:03:06,400
[UMALI CHUCKLES]

61
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:09,633
What's with you?

62
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,200
There's so many of these,

63
00:03:12,333 --> 00:03:14,533
you think they'll notice
we took a few?

64
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:17,133
It's just for fun!

65
00:03:18,433 --> 00:03:19,467
[POLICE] Stand up!

66
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,167
[ARTURO] Sir, ma'am.

67
00:03:22,967 --> 00:03:26,433
I have bad news.
Our warehouse in Inustre...

68
00:03:26,533 --> 00:03:29,267
- The NLEA raided it.
- A raid?!

69
00:03:29,367 --> 00:03:30,833
They have
a search warrant, ma'am.

70
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,433
Someone reported
that we mine gold illegally.

71
00:03:34,533 --> 00:03:37,500
- What did they take?
- All of our gold.

72
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,667
NLEA. It's NLEA again!

73
00:03:42,833 --> 00:03:46,300
I'm certain
Ricardo is behind all this!

74
00:03:46,433 --> 00:03:50,300
Pa, this isn't just a raid.
They want war!

75
00:03:50,433 --> 00:03:53,667
Tell me where
I can find the Jacintos.

76
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:55,833
I'll kill every single one
of them.

77
00:03:56,033 --> 00:03:58,633
I'll come with you.

78
00:04:01,733 --> 00:04:03,867
Ma'am, I'll take this
to the crime lab.

79
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:06,267
Tell them to expedite
the process, okay?

80
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,700
- Okay, ma'am.
- Alright, alright.

81
00:04:07,833 --> 00:04:09,033
- Lieutenant!
- Sir.

82
00:04:10,533 --> 00:04:12,767
We recovered shell casings
in Estuary One

83
00:04:12,900 --> 00:04:15,367
that match the empty shells
we saw on Soriano Street.

84
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:16,867
Did you have
Ballistics check it?

85
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:17,867
Yes, sir.

86
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,200
We're just waiting
for the results.

87
00:04:19,333 --> 00:04:22,833
If it's a confirmed match,
we have a second contact point.

88
00:04:22,967 --> 00:04:25,367
It's possible the shooting began
on Soriano Street

89
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:26,833
and reached Estuary One.

90
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,700
But we're not sure
if Sam was involved in this.

91
00:04:29,833 --> 00:04:33,200
And if she's the one chasing
or she's the one being chased.

92
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:36,467
I'm only sure of one thing, sir.

93
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:39,067
Sam fought until the end.

94
00:04:41,667 --> 00:04:44,567
It's possible Estuary One was
her escape route.

95
00:04:44,733 --> 00:04:47,133
You look into
that possibility, lieutenant.

96
00:04:47,267 --> 00:04:48,167
Copy, sir.

97
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,700
Ma'am Pia?

98
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:55,567
Uh...

99
00:04:56,267 --> 00:04:57,200
Why did you call for me?

100
00:04:57,333 --> 00:05:03,567
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

101
00:05:03,733 --> 00:05:05,100
[DOOR CREAKS SHUT]

102
00:05:11,267 --> 00:05:13,567
There is something
important you need to know.

103
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:17,767
I will only entrust
this information to you.

104
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:20,267
Based on your track record...

105
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:24,033
You are the only one
I can 100% trust.

106
00:05:24,933 --> 00:05:28,933
The Zafras have a spy
within the NCIA.

107
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:32,700
I need your help
to find out who that is.

108
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:36,100
I know that traitor is working
for the Zafras,

109
00:05:36,267 --> 00:05:38,567
all the while we're searching
for Jacinto.

110
00:05:38,667 --> 00:05:40,467
You cannot tell anyone
about this.

111
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:43,267
And we cannot trust
anyone else.

112
00:05:44,167 --> 00:05:46,467
- At least for now.
- Even Sir Seb?

113
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,567
Yes, everyone.

114
00:05:47,667 --> 00:05:51,467
Even a member of Team Alpha
can be a spy.

115
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,700
If you notice
anything suspicious,

116
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:55,633
report it to me right away.

117
00:05:57,267 --> 00:05:58,633
You are my only ally for now.

118
00:05:58,767 --> 00:06:00,133
Are you sure
of what you're saying?

119
00:06:00,267 --> 00:06:03,633
[HUSHED] Shh! Don't be too loud!
They might hear you!

120
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,867
That's what we have
to find out.

121
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,567
We'll have to make
that traitor pay.

122
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:11,500
I understand, Pia.

123
00:06:11,633 --> 00:06:15,800
I know you're trying to help me
because you're hurting for me

124
00:06:15,933 --> 00:06:17,600
because Sam is missing,
but you have to understand--

125
00:06:17,700 --> 00:06:19,467
Please, Sebastian.

126
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:22,400
I won't compete
with someone who's missing.

127
00:06:22,533 --> 00:06:24,500
Don't call it a competition.

128
00:06:24,633 --> 00:06:26,467
I don't want people fighting
over me.

129
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:28,933
Pia, I have a lot
of important things to do,

130
00:06:29,033 --> 00:06:31,633
so we should just focus
on finding Sam!

131
00:06:31,767 --> 00:06:34,933
When she returns,
then you choose.

132
00:06:36,433 --> 00:06:37,967
I'm not in a hurry, anyway.

133
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:41,833
Team, conference room meeting
with Sir Delgado in 5 minutes.

134
00:06:42,033 --> 00:06:48,833
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:06:48,967 --> 00:06:51,200
[DELGADO] So, Sebastian...

136
00:06:52,333 --> 00:06:55,333
What's your plan
for the ongoing search for Sam?

137
00:06:56,367 --> 00:06:59,833
Sir, we did our initial research
in the area yesterday.

138
00:06:59,967 --> 00:07:02,133
The next step is to expand
the perimeter

139
00:07:02,233 --> 00:07:04,700
by two kilometers
from the last known location.

140
00:07:04,833 --> 00:07:05,933
- Hm.
- [PIA] So...

141
00:07:06,067 --> 00:07:10,000
You'll split Team Alpha
into groups for the search?

142
00:07:10,133 --> 00:07:13,300
[SEBASTIAN] Yes. It's important
we speed up our efforts

143
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,833
in searching for Sam.

144
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,800
Besides, other agents are
also focused on this,

145
00:07:16,933 --> 00:07:19,400
- not just Team Alpha.
- Sir.

146
00:07:19,567 --> 00:07:20,967
- [DELGADO] Yes?
- Can I give a suggestion

147
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:23,167
- for the investigation?
- What are you thinking?

148
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:24,900
What if...

149
00:07:26,733 --> 00:07:30,067
Um, you shuffle your groups.

150
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,300
I mean...

151
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:36,400
You might come up
with a different idea...

152
00:07:37,767 --> 00:07:40,000
...when you're discussing
with someone new.

153
00:07:42,433 --> 00:07:45,867
Like, someone who's not
usually your partner.

154
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,467
But then again,
it's just a suggestion.

155
00:07:48,633 --> 00:07:52,100
Well, team?
Any violent reactions?

156
00:07:55,133 --> 00:07:57,667
None? Then shuffle is in order.

157
00:07:59,367 --> 00:08:06,200
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

158
00:08:08,033 --> 00:08:09,333
- [SIGHS]
- [DOOR OPENS]

159
00:08:09,467 --> 00:08:10,600
Ma'am! Ma'am!

160
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:12,667
The ballistics report has
come out.

161
00:08:13,367 --> 00:08:14,267
[MAX] It's confirmed.

162
00:08:14,467 --> 00:08:16,233
The bullets found at First Creek
and Soriano Street

163
00:08:16,367 --> 00:08:17,500
came from the same gun.

164
00:08:17,633 --> 00:08:18,600
[DOOR OPENS]

165
00:08:18,733 --> 00:08:20,067
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

166
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,033
Ma'am, we just got back
from NCIA.

167
00:08:22,167 --> 00:08:24,267
Here's the complete list of
cases your sister was handling

168
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,300
in the last six months.

169
00:08:26,467 --> 00:08:27,900
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

170
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,233
Looks like her most
high-profile case was...

171
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:38,133
...alias Tiger's.

172
00:08:40,433 --> 00:08:42,133
Victor Zafra...

173
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,567
<i>You don't know the person
you're up against.</i>

174
00:08:44,667 --> 00:08:45,633
<i> He's a powerful man.</i>

175
00:08:45,767 --> 00:08:47,767
<i>Dad, he exchanged fire
with the NCIA.</i>

176
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,633
<i>And he's been doing
illegal transactions.</i>

177
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,300
<i>The Zafras are operating
legitimate businesses.</i>

178
00:08:51,467 --> 00:08:53,267
<i>What illegal transactions
are you talking about?</i>

179
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,033
<i>He's the leader of the
gold-smuggling syndicate!</i>

180
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,333
<i>I heard Mr. Chan died
in that ambush.</i>

181
00:08:57,467 --> 00:08:59,567
<i>Is that the case Dad
wanted you to drop?</i>

182
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:02,600
<i> Well, I can't just let the
</i>criminals who did this go free.

183
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:07,167
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:09:07,333 --> 00:09:10,333
I'm sure the Zafras are behind
Sam's disappearance.

185
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,067
Come on.

186
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:17,567
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:21,000
[ALL TEASING, CLAPPING]

188
00:09:21,167 --> 00:09:22,933
- So perfect for each other!
- What a lovely couple!

189
00:09:23,033 --> 00:09:25,900
- Move aside, Tekla!
- Oh, don't push me!

190
00:09:26,033 --> 00:09:28,600
- You hit the jackpot, Gabo!
- Careful now.

191
00:09:28,733 --> 00:09:30,633
- Tekla, you'll let her win?
- Well?

192
00:09:30,733 --> 00:09:32,367
We're not even playing
the same game!

193
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:33,633
- Totally!
- I'm way better!

194
00:09:33,733 --> 00:09:35,800
- Psst! Keep it down!
- Like, she just stood there!

195
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,033
- [SCOFFS]
- [RUDY CLEARS THROAT]

196
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,267
Gabo.

197
00:09:38,633 --> 00:09:40,200
It's my birthday, remember?

198
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:41,133
[GABO CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

199
00:09:41,233 --> 00:09:42,533
Sorry, Pa.

200
00:09:43,033 --> 00:09:46,467
I just can't take my eyes
off my wife because...

201
00:09:46,567 --> 00:09:48,200
[LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

202
00:09:48,333 --> 00:09:49,533
she's so beautiful.

203
00:09:49,667 --> 00:09:52,267
[ALL SQUEALING]

204
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:53,533
- Fight back, sister!
- Yeah!

205
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:54,967
- Rudy...
- Hmm?

206
00:09:55,067 --> 00:09:57,200
- [BONG] Quiet!
- Today is your birthday.

207
00:09:57,367 --> 00:10:01,000
But soon, we might be
attending a baptism.

208
00:10:01,667 --> 00:10:03,733
- [BONG] You know it!
- [BINOY] Oh my!

209
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:05,067
[TEKLA] Miss Mameng!

210
00:10:05,233 --> 00:10:06,167
Most likely.

211
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:08,400
Hey, love...

212
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,167
Did you hear that?

213
00:10:10,767 --> 00:10:12,467
It sounds like my father's...

214
00:10:12,867 --> 00:10:15,400
looking forward
to his grandchild.

215
00:10:15,533 --> 00:10:16,400
[DABOY SQUEALS, CLAPS]

216
00:10:16,567 --> 00:10:17,633
Stop it!

217
00:10:17,767 --> 00:10:20,467
Look at them, all lovey-dovey.

218
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:22,067
Anyway, aren't we going
to eat now?

219
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,167
Yes! Hang on!

220
00:10:23,333 --> 00:10:25,400
That's absolutely true!
Daddy, I brought you cake!

221
00:10:25,567 --> 00:10:27,533
- For your birthday!
- Hey, hey!

222
00:10:27,667 --> 00:10:29,133
- Because I love you!
- Come on now!

223
00:10:29,267 --> 00:10:30,400
No!

224
00:10:30,567 --> 00:10:33,233
- [MAMENG] Come on, let's eat!
- Everyone, grab a plate or two!

225
00:10:33,367 --> 00:10:35,633
[CHEERING]

226
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:42,733
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER, CLAPPING]

227
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:47,067
[TOLITS, IN SINGSONG VOICE]
<i> Oh, my heart...</i>

228
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:54,167
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" BY
JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

229
00:11:11,933 --> 00:11:17,767
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]
- [BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:11:21,233 --> 00:11:23,300
Mister Badong!

231
00:11:23,433 --> 00:11:25,133
Hey! Mister Badong is back!

232
00:11:25,267 --> 00:11:26,467
[LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

233
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:29,200
- Mister Badong!
- He's out of the hospital!

234
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:31,367
Mister Badong,
are you doing fine now?

235
00:11:32,233 --> 00:11:33,733
- Badong.
- Mister Rudy.

236
00:11:33,833 --> 00:11:35,800
- How are you feeling, Badong?
- I'm good, Mister Rudy.

237
00:11:35,967 --> 00:11:39,200
Just some minor sprains
and a cut on the head.

238
00:11:39,333 --> 00:11:41,367
I'm sorry.
You fell from our roof.

239
00:11:41,533 --> 00:11:42,500
No worries, Mister Rudy.

240
00:11:42,667 --> 00:11:45,433
It was my fault
for losing balance anyway.

241
00:11:45,533 --> 00:11:47,300
That's nothing.
He's built differently.

242
00:11:47,433 --> 00:11:49,067
- He can take anything.
- Hey, hey!

243
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:51,400
You should join your family
and eat with us.

244
00:11:51,533 --> 00:11:52,433
Thank you.

245
00:11:52,533 --> 00:11:53,833
Let's eat, Mister Badong!

246
00:11:53,967 --> 00:11:55,167
- I'll assist him.
- Slow and steady!

247
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,567
Mister Badong, join us!

248
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:58,233
[BINOY] Mister Badong,
is that a bald spot now?

249
00:11:58,367 --> 00:12:00,233
[TOLITS] Oh, please!
Don't ask him that!

250
00:12:00,367 --> 00:12:01,433
I don't like that!

251
00:12:01,533 --> 00:12:03,333
[LIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

252
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,433
I'm glad he's still alright.

253
00:12:06,933 --> 00:12:08,333
Well, love...

254
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:10,167
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

255
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:11,967
It's all thanks to you.

256
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,067
If it weren't for you,

257
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,133
who knows what might've
happened to Mister Badong.

258
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:17,367
[DANTE] That's true.
You know, Gloria...

259
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,533
it was you who saved
Badong's life.

260
00:12:20,567 --> 00:12:22,167
Oh, it's no big deal.

261
00:12:22,300 --> 00:12:23,533
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

262
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,200
[MAMENG] Come on, eat up.

263
00:12:27,833 --> 00:12:29,333
[RUDY] Let's eat, everyone.

264
00:12:29,467 --> 00:12:31,033
- Happy birthday.
- Don't be shy now.

265
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:32,200
- Join us.
- Happy birthday.

266
00:12:32,333 --> 00:12:34,167
- Mmm, thanks.
- Thank you.

267
00:12:35,567 --> 00:12:37,700
- Melchor, what did you get?
- [UMALI] Sir.

268
00:12:37,867 --> 00:12:39,700
We have over 50 kilos
of gold bars,

269
00:12:39,833 --> 00:12:42,100
transaction ledgers, and
receipts in our possession.

270
00:12:42,233 --> 00:12:44,533
Bring all the confiscated items
to the evidence room.

271
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,200
I'll inform General Jacinto.

272
00:12:46,333 --> 00:12:47,267
- Yes, sir.
- Alright.

273
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,667
Listen, process them now!

274
00:12:48,833 --> 00:12:50,300
- Yes, sir.
- Move it!

275
00:12:50,433 --> 00:12:51,967
- Come on!
- Follow us!

276
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:54,033
- Remember what I told you.
- This way!

277
00:12:54,167 --> 00:12:55,367
Keep in mind your stations.

278
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:56,700
Alright then, go ahead.

279
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:58,167
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

280
00:12:58,267 --> 00:12:59,533
Sir, what's with those guys?

281
00:12:59,667 --> 00:13:01,567
We raided the Zafras' warehouse.

282
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:03,367
A firefight broke out
soon after, but...

283
00:13:03,500 --> 00:13:05,233
we managed to arrest
those working for them.

284
00:13:06,067 --> 00:13:07,900
[SANTOS]
Sir, let's file the report.

285
00:13:08,033 --> 00:13:08,900
Let's go.

286
00:13:15,667 --> 00:13:17,900
[DOOR SLIDING]

287
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:20,233
[PHONE RINGING]

288
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:21,467
[GLASS THUDS]

289
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,100
Domingo.

290
00:13:23,233 --> 00:13:24,167
General Jacinto,

291
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:26,000
we've carried out your order.

292
00:13:26,133 --> 00:13:27,933
What happened?
Did you get anything?

293
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:29,233
Were any goons arrested?

294
00:13:29,367 --> 00:13:30,267
<i> Some fought back, sir.</i>

295
00:13:30,467 --> 00:13:32,233
<i>But they've been brought
to the police station.</i>

296
00:13:32,367 --> 00:13:35,600
<i>We also recovered
three crates of gold bars,</i>

297
00:13:35,733 --> 00:13:37,667
<i> along with jewelry</i>

298
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:39,400
and transaction ledgers.

299
00:13:39,533 --> 00:13:41,100
We're just sorting out
the inventory.

300
00:13:41,233 --> 00:13:42,333
Secure the gold.

301
00:13:42,467 --> 00:13:44,567
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

302
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:48,100
This is just the beginning
of the Zafras' downfall.

303
00:13:50,133 --> 00:13:51,000
[PHONE CLATTERS]

304
00:13:51,133 --> 00:13:52,033
Boss...

305
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,400
What's your plan after all this?

306
00:13:56,800 --> 00:14:00,200
We'll have an easier time
finding Sam...

307
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,800
since the Zafras are tied up
with their business troubles.

308
00:14:03,967 --> 00:14:11,033
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

309
00:14:11,467 --> 00:14:12,700
[MUSIC ENDS]

310
00:14:12,833 --> 00:14:13,800
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

311
00:14:14,267 --> 00:14:15,567
- [DEBORAH] Wait, wait, wait!
- Take this.

312
00:14:15,667 --> 00:14:16,300
What the heck?

313
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:18,200
Are we seriously
doing this again?

314
00:14:18,333 --> 00:14:20,133
You keep rushing in
without thinking!

315
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:21,467
Calm down!

316
00:14:22,733 --> 00:14:23,967
Let us all...

317
00:14:24,433 --> 00:14:26,367
calm down.

318
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:28,233
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

319
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:29,600
Okay.

320
00:14:30,033 --> 00:14:33,333
So Ricado is hitting us
where it hurts,

321
00:14:33,467 --> 00:14:36,000
but let's not give him
the satisfaction.

322
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:37,767
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

323
00:14:37,867 --> 00:14:39,267
What?

324
00:14:39,367 --> 00:14:42,167
Are we just going to let him do
whatever he wants against us?

325
00:14:42,333 --> 00:14:44,633
[LUCAS]
We should retaliate, Ma!

326
00:14:44,767 --> 00:14:45,633
[SCOFFS]

327
00:14:45,767 --> 00:14:47,167
Of course not!

328
00:14:48,033 --> 00:14:51,333
Because that's exactly
what Ricardo wants.

329
00:14:51,933 --> 00:14:53,600
He's cornering us

330
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:56,300
so we'll be forced
to fight back.

331
00:14:56,433 --> 00:15:00,333
He's trying to find a way
to send us all behind bars.

332
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,833
We're not going
to fight him now.

333
00:15:04,033 --> 00:15:06,667
But we do need to recover

334
00:15:07,233 --> 00:15:10,367
the gold bars that were taken
from us by NLEA.

335
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:12,767
We'll let others handle it.

336
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:17,367
People who can't be
traced back to us

337
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:18,667
if things go south.

338
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,100
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

339
00:15:20,233 --> 00:15:21,367
[MARIANO] I got this.

340
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,633
I know some people.

341
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:28,433
- I'll just talk to them.
- Go on, ma'am.

342
00:15:28,567 --> 00:15:29,533
Get them on their feet.

343
00:15:29,867 --> 00:15:30,867
Get up!

344
00:15:31,033 --> 00:15:32,600
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:15:32,733 --> 00:15:34,167
Do you work for the Zafras?

346
00:15:35,367 --> 00:15:37,367
Did you also ambush my sister?

347
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:41,200
Answer me!

348
00:15:41,333 --> 00:15:42,233
Why?

349
00:15:42,533 --> 00:15:43,467
Is she dead?

350
00:15:44,533 --> 00:15:45,233
Come here!

351
00:15:45,433 --> 00:15:47,900
- Ma'am! Ma'am! Ma'am!
- You bastard!

352
00:15:48,067 --> 00:15:49,067
[MAX PANTS]

353
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:51,300
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

354
00:15:51,433 --> 00:15:53,667
If anything happened
to my sister...

355
00:15:56,267 --> 00:15:58,400
I would come after every
single one of you.

356
00:16:05,533 --> 00:16:06,167
Hello?

357
00:16:06,333 --> 00:16:08,533
Mr. Zafra wants to speak
with you.

358
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:10,500
- Sir.
- [GLASS THUDS]

359
00:16:12,533 --> 00:16:13,433
Paquito.

360
00:16:13,567 --> 00:16:14,600
Boss Mariano!

361
00:16:15,633 --> 00:16:16,600
How may I help you?

362
00:16:16,733 --> 00:16:17,400
<i> You know why</i>

363
00:16:17,567 --> 00:16:19,100
I called you
in the first place.

364
00:16:19,267 --> 00:16:20,433
- Of course.
- [MUG THUDS]

365
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:22,600
You want me
to hunt someone down.

366
00:16:22,933 --> 00:16:24,233
Let's meet.

367
00:16:24,567 --> 00:16:26,533
Where? When?

368
00:16:26,933 --> 00:16:29,700
Arturo will send you
the details.

369
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:32,267
Okay, boss! Welcome back!

370
00:16:32,433 --> 00:16:33,267
[LAUGHS]

371
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:38,433
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

372
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:39,500
[PAQUITO] Django!

373
00:16:40,867 --> 00:16:43,433
Mariano Zafra called.

374
00:16:44,167 --> 00:16:46,767
He's got a job for us.

375
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:48,133
Zafra?

376
00:16:48,267 --> 00:16:51,300
The same person who ordered
the hit on the congressman?

377
00:16:51,467 --> 00:16:55,033
He's also the reason
why Gabo was imprisoned.

378
00:16:55,167 --> 00:16:56,467
So, what's the job?

379
00:16:56,833 --> 00:16:57,967
Is the pay any good?

380
00:16:58,133 --> 00:16:59,200
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

381
00:16:59,333 --> 00:17:01,200
There are no details yet.

382
00:17:01,333 --> 00:17:04,933
But, we will meet
with them today.

383
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:09,367
As long as the money's fat,
we're all in.

384
00:17:11,333 --> 00:17:13,600
Dudo, get the crew ready.
We're heading out.

385
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:15,267
Okay, boss.

386
00:17:15,433 --> 00:17:16,833
Hey, let's get ready.

387
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:21,067
- [SANTOS] Sir.
- [EXHALES HEAVILY]

388
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:23,833
Max's sister has been missing
for two days.

389
00:17:24,367 --> 00:17:25,500
She's probably dead!

390
00:17:26,267 --> 00:17:27,500
No doubt about it!

391
00:17:27,667 --> 00:17:28,567
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

392
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:29,733
Santos!

393
00:17:30,167 --> 00:17:31,167
What did you say?!

394
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,233
- [GRUNTS]
- [BLOW LANDS]

395
00:17:32,367 --> 00:17:34,167
- My sister is still alive!
- That's enough!

396
00:17:34,333 --> 00:17:35,167
- Ma'am!
- Get off me!

397
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:37,167
- What's going--
- Without a body...

398
00:17:37,333 --> 00:17:39,333
- Enough! Stop this!
- ...she's not dead yet!

399
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,333
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]
- [SANTOS GROANS]

400
00:17:41,767 --> 00:17:45,167
[MAX PANTING]

401
00:17:45,333 --> 00:17:47,633
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

402
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:48,767
[SANTOS EXHALES WEAKLY]

403
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:50,500
[MAX BREATHING SHARPLY]

404
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:58,333
- [PANICKED BREATHING]
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:17:59,667 --> 00:18:00,633
[MAX GRUNTS]

406
00:18:00,733 --> 00:18:02,000
[EXCLAIMING]

407
00:18:02,133 --> 00:18:05,000
- [BANGING ON WINDOW]
- [SCREAMING]

408
00:18:05,133 --> 00:18:12,167
[MAX BREATHING HEAVILY]

409
00:18:12,733 --> 00:18:19,667
[SOBBING]

410
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:26,633
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

411
00:18:37,233 --> 00:18:38,733
You know
your designated positions.

412
00:18:38,867 --> 00:18:40,467
Guys, don't blow your cover.

413
00:18:40,567 --> 00:18:42,900
We need to find Sam.
Good luck, team.

414
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:46,700
[VENDOR] They're so shameless!

415
00:18:46,833 --> 00:18:48,633
[SEQIOA] Perfect,
I'm getting hungry.

416
00:18:49,333 --> 00:18:50,633
- I'll have this.
- That's ten pesos.

417
00:18:50,767 --> 00:18:52,700
[MAN] You've been at it
since earlier!

418
00:18:52,833 --> 00:18:54,067
[INDISTINCT CHATTERING]

419
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:55,800
Miss.

420
00:18:55,967 --> 00:18:58,067
That shootout that happened
on Soriano Street was brutal.

421
00:18:58,200 --> 00:19:00,867
Have you heard about what
happened to the victim?

422
00:19:01,033 --> 00:19:01,933
No.

423
00:19:02,533 --> 00:19:03,767
But, you know,

424
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:06,333
that thing normally happens
around here.

425
00:19:06,467 --> 00:19:08,833
Are you going to buy more?
Come on, this is good.

426
00:19:08,967 --> 00:19:10,100
[SEBASTIAN] Ma'am.

427
00:19:10,233 --> 00:19:12,267
Have you heard about what
happened in Soriano Street

428
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,333
the other day?

429
00:19:13,433 --> 00:19:14,600
[WOMAN] What?

430
00:19:14,733 --> 00:19:16,933
I just wanted to know
if you've heard

431
00:19:17,067 --> 00:19:19,200
about what happened
in Soriano Street.

432
00:19:19,367 --> 00:19:21,000
Huh? I can't hear you.

433
00:19:21,133 --> 00:19:24,200
You didn't hear
anything about it?

434
00:19:24,367 --> 00:19:25,533
What?

435
00:19:26,100 --> 00:19:28,500
Nothing. Thank you.
We're about to arrive.

436
00:19:28,633 --> 00:19:29,767
What did you say?

437
00:19:30,967 --> 00:19:32,700
This one's hopeless.

438
00:19:33,067 --> 00:19:36,033
Mister, was there
another commotion

439
00:19:36,167 --> 00:19:38,533
after the shootout
in Soriano Street?

440
00:19:38,667 --> 00:19:40,267
What commotion?

441
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,400
Oh, no, mister.

442
00:19:41,567 --> 00:19:43,133
What he meant was

443
00:19:43,267 --> 00:19:45,300
we have a female friend
who got into a fight here.

444
00:19:45,433 --> 00:19:46,700
She's a newcomer.

445
00:19:46,833 --> 00:19:47,900
We're wondering if you've
heard about it.

446
00:19:48,067 --> 00:19:49,767
Fights happen here every day.

447
00:19:50,233 --> 00:19:52,700
A simple game
could turn into a full brawl.

448
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:54,400
So what fight
are you talking about?

449
00:19:54,567 --> 00:19:58,200
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

450
00:19:58,333 --> 00:20:00,200
- [MAN 1] That's a lot.
- You should go there.

451
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:01,533
[MAN 2] It's tails!

452
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:02,633
- I win.
- Yeah.

453
00:20:02,767 --> 00:20:04,500
Miss, you need anything?

454
00:20:04,633 --> 00:20:07,233
My brother and I are
looking for a house for rent.

455
00:20:07,333 --> 00:20:08,233
Do you know a place?

456
00:20:08,367 --> 00:20:09,333
House for rent?

457
00:20:09,833 --> 00:20:10,833
Do you guys know a place?

458
00:20:10,967 --> 00:20:12,733
- No.
- No?

459
00:20:12,867 --> 00:20:13,967
[MAN 2] Your turn.

460
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:15,400
[MAN 3] Okay. I'll bet 20 pesos.

461
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:16,500
[MAN 1] This is Rommel's.

462
00:20:16,967 --> 00:20:18,133
[COINS CLINK]

463
00:20:18,833 --> 00:20:20,100
[MARIANO] Paquito.

464
00:20:20,767 --> 00:20:22,267
[PAQUITO] Boss Mariano.

465
00:20:22,633 --> 00:20:24,433
Long time, short time.

466
00:20:26,100 --> 00:20:27,667
Do you remember Romy?

467
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:28,733
Boss.

468
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:32,067
This is my son, Django.

469
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:36,400
He is now the King of Tondo.

470
00:20:36,900 --> 00:20:37,767
Let's all get seated.

471
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:44,867
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

472
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,967
- I'm nervous, Pa.
- Why?

473
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:56,667
The liquor is expensive.
My throat isn't used to it.

474
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:59,800
[LAUGHING]

475
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:01,500
[PAQUITO] Then we should try it.

476
00:21:03,233 --> 00:21:05,667
- Ah! It's good!
- Delicious! [CHUCKLES]

477
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,833
You know what
the Americans say?

478
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,800
It's better to lose
a thousand of women

479
00:21:09,933 --> 00:21:11,500
than a single drop of wine.

480
00:21:11,667 --> 00:21:12,867
[CHUCKLING]

481
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,567
What do you want us to do?

482
00:21:14,700 --> 00:21:21,567
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

483
00:21:22,267 --> 00:21:23,867
Imported liquors are different.

484
00:21:26,167 --> 00:21:27,800
This is what
you're going to do.

485
00:21:27,933 --> 00:21:30,467
NLEA raided our warehouse.

486
00:21:30,567 --> 00:21:32,033
They stole our gold.

487
00:21:32,167 --> 00:21:33,333
Since I worked in NLEA before,

488
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:37,067
I know which safe house they
bring that kind of evidence.

489
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:40,633
You want us to take the gold
from the safe house?

490
00:21:40,733 --> 00:21:42,367
Not in the safe house.

491
00:21:42,533 --> 00:21:44,067
You have to steal the gold

492
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:46,067
before it gets to
the safe house.

493
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:47,767
That's the address
of the safe house

494
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:49,933
from the NLEA precinct.

495
00:21:50,067 --> 00:21:51,867
It's possible that the vehicle
carrying the gold

496
00:21:52,033 --> 00:21:52,933
will take that route.

497
00:21:53,067 --> 00:21:55,600
You need to make it look
like it's robbery.

498
00:21:55,733 --> 00:21:58,433
You can't make it obvious
that I ordered you to do it.

499
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:00,667
Sixth precinct.

500
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:04,100
A person from the sixth precinct
will bring the gold?

501
00:22:04,233 --> 00:22:08,333
The sixth precinct
raided our warehouse.

502
00:22:11,367 --> 00:22:13,867
If we can give
the gold back to you,

503
00:22:14,033 --> 00:22:15,100
what will we get in return?

504
00:22:15,267 --> 00:22:17,200
We will pay you generously.

505
00:22:17,667 --> 00:22:18,567
How generous?

506
00:22:23,400 --> 00:22:25,800
Here's 100,000. That's just
for the down payment.

507
00:22:25,933 --> 00:22:27,867
You're asking us to steal gold.

508
00:22:27,967 --> 00:22:30,100
We're going to go
against NLEA.

509
00:22:30,233 --> 00:22:32,200
And you're only paying us
100,000 as a down payment?

510
00:22:32,300 --> 00:22:33,067
Django.

511
00:22:33,233 --> 00:22:35,700
No, Pa.
This is a dangerous mission.

512
00:22:35,833 --> 00:22:37,367
And they'll only pay us
that much?

513
00:22:37,500 --> 00:22:39,067
Do they think
we're just small fries?

514
00:22:39,233 --> 00:22:41,433
Give us 200,000
for the down payment

515
00:22:42,067 --> 00:22:43,900
and I will deliver you
the gold myself.

516
00:22:44,067 --> 00:22:51,067
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

517
00:22:55,700 --> 00:22:57,633
If you keep this up,

518
00:22:57,767 --> 00:22:59,433
we're going to get along.

519
00:23:01,333 --> 00:23:02,000
[CHUCKLES]

520
00:23:02,433 --> 00:23:04,133
I'm at your service, boss.

521
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:07,400
[CACKLING]

522
00:23:07,533 --> 00:23:08,567
[LUCAS] Ma.

523
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,067
Where's Papa?

524
00:23:10,200 --> 00:23:11,633
He's outside. He has a meeting.

525
00:23:12,267 --> 00:23:13,067
Who?

526
00:23:13,633 --> 00:23:15,067
Some of our former men.

527
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:17,800
He said he has something
important for them to do.

528
00:23:17,933 --> 00:23:19,567
Why didn't he ask me to do it?

529
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,967
Whatever it is, I can do it, Ma.

530
00:23:22,133 --> 00:23:25,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

531
00:23:25,567 --> 00:23:26,767
Lucas.

532
00:23:27,800 --> 00:23:31,133
Don't think that your father
doesn't trust you.

533
00:23:31,300 --> 00:23:32,700
I was the one who told him

534
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:34,867
to get people outside our group.

535
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:39,100
NCIA and NLEA already
have their eyes on us.

536
00:23:39,233 --> 00:23:41,533
And don't forget
Ricardo Jacinto.

537
00:23:41,667 --> 00:23:43,167
He's out to get us.

538
00:23:44,900 --> 00:23:46,767
We need outsiders

539
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:48,833
to do the dirty job for us.

540
00:23:49,167 --> 00:23:52,333
So when things get messy
and risky,

541
00:23:52,467 --> 00:23:55,033
they're the ones taking
the fall, not our group.

542
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:03,467
- [DJANGO] Pa.
- [PAQUITO GRUNTS]

543
00:24:04,567 --> 00:24:09,033
We're getting 200,000 pesos
just for the down payment.

544
00:24:09,167 --> 00:24:10,900
Whatever Gabo does

545
00:24:11,033 --> 00:24:12,700
to earn that much money,

546
00:24:12,833 --> 00:24:14,900
it won't compare to what
we're going to earn from this.

547
00:24:15,033 --> 00:24:16,033
[CACKLES]

548
00:24:16,167 --> 00:24:19,000
But the sixth precinct...

549
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:21,300
It's Domingo's men.

550
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:26,067
And I'm sure Umali
and Santos will handle it.

551
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:28,200
We're going to go
against NLEA?

552
00:24:28,333 --> 00:24:30,467
We've been tight-knit with them
for a long time.

553
00:24:31,700 --> 00:24:32,867
That's the problem, Pa.

554
00:24:33,700 --> 00:24:36,100
We've been working
with them for a long time,

555
00:24:36,233 --> 00:24:38,667
but they're not paying us a lot.

556
00:24:38,800 --> 00:24:40,500
At the right price,

557
00:24:40,867 --> 00:24:42,933
I can easily drop them.

558
00:24:43,067 --> 00:24:45,067
Easy there, Django.

559
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:47,533
It's not just about money.

560
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:49,033
They're our protectors.

561
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:51,567
And our connection with NLEA

562
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:54,100
is a huge advantage to us.

563
00:24:54,233 --> 00:24:57,100
But Django already has
the money.

564
00:24:57,233 --> 00:24:58,833
Don't tell me you're backing out
on the Zafras.

565
00:24:58,967 --> 00:25:00,733
Since when did I say no
to blessings?

566
00:25:02,233 --> 00:25:04,800
Django, you take care of this.

567
00:25:04,933 --> 00:25:06,467
But make sure

568
00:25:06,833 --> 00:25:09,367
that NLEA won't recognize you.

569
00:25:10,967 --> 00:25:12,733
I know what to do, Pa.

570
00:25:13,233 --> 00:25:14,533
[CACKLES]

571
00:25:14,900 --> 00:25:15,800
Here.

572
00:25:16,900 --> 00:25:17,933
You little...

573
00:25:18,067 --> 00:25:19,467
Even if we're friends,

574
00:25:19,600 --> 00:25:21,233
I wouldn't take your side
on that.

575
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:22,867
What were you thinking?

576
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:24,367
I didn't know she would hear it.

577
00:25:24,467 --> 00:25:26,933
Santos, let me remind you.

578
00:25:27,067 --> 00:25:30,533
This is about
General Jacinto's daughter.

579
00:25:30,633 --> 00:25:31,800
I'm sorry, sir.

580
00:25:31,933 --> 00:25:34,400
Keep your thoughts
to yourself.

581
00:25:34,567 --> 00:25:36,567
You can't just blurt things out,

582
00:25:36,767 --> 00:25:39,133
especially when
there is no evidence.

583
00:25:39,267 --> 00:25:40,467
I won't do it again, sir.

584
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:41,500
Okay.

585
00:25:41,933 --> 00:25:43,233
Back to work.

586
00:25:45,500 --> 00:25:47,733
So, how are we
going to do it?

587
00:25:48,433 --> 00:25:51,233
I'm sure they reached out
to us

588
00:25:51,367 --> 00:25:53,833
because they didn't want
their group to get involved

589
00:25:53,967 --> 00:25:55,467
when things go south.

590
00:25:55,600 --> 00:25:58,267
If that's the case, then
we need to hire others

591
00:25:58,433 --> 00:25:59,600
to take the fall for us.

592
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:02,067
I'll talk to Gabo.

593
00:26:02,167 --> 00:26:03,667
So if things don't go
according to plan,

594
00:26:04,100 --> 00:26:05,167
he'll have to take the blame.

595
00:26:05,300 --> 00:26:07,600
Boss, he has probably learned
his lesson back then.

596
00:26:07,767 --> 00:26:09,167
When he went to jail.

597
00:26:09,333 --> 00:26:11,200
I'm starting to get
on his good side again.

598
00:26:11,333 --> 00:26:14,267
Besides, that guy
hasn't changed at all.

599
00:26:14,367 --> 00:26:15,967
He's still doing the dirty work
for others.

600
00:26:16,133 --> 00:26:18,767
But I'm just earning
a lot more than him.

601
00:26:19,867 --> 00:26:22,833
He earns 200,000 for one job.

602
00:26:23,300 --> 00:26:25,333
That just what I get
for down payment.

603
00:26:25,467 --> 00:26:27,767
- Impressive!
- So he'll definitely agree.

604
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:30,200
And it's Rudy's birthday.

605
00:26:30,333 --> 00:26:32,167
We will go there
and talk to them.

606
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:34,800
I can take care
of Gabo myself, Pa.

607
00:26:34,967 --> 00:26:36,033
Why do you have to be there?

608
00:26:36,167 --> 00:26:38,933
You take care of Gabo.

609
00:26:39,067 --> 00:26:40,267
While I...

610
00:26:41,067 --> 00:26:42,267
will take care of someone else.

611
00:26:42,900 --> 00:26:44,367
Is it Betchay?

612
00:26:44,500 --> 00:26:46,967
I don't know if you're
really serious about her.

613
00:26:47,067 --> 00:26:49,300
Well, you know, Django,

614
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:52,667
I just want to prove
that Betchay made a mistake

615
00:26:52,833 --> 00:26:54,967
by choosing Rudy over me.

616
00:26:55,100 --> 00:26:57,167
Betchay is deeply in love
with Rudy.

617
00:26:57,333 --> 00:26:59,000
I don't think that'll change
any time soon.

618
00:26:59,167 --> 00:27:02,400
I don't care how deep,
I'm diving in.

619
00:27:02,833 --> 00:27:03,900
[CHUCKLES]

620
00:27:04,033 --> 00:27:06,667
Your father
never runs out of quips.

621
00:27:06,833 --> 00:27:07,700
[DJANGO] Take this along.

622
00:27:07,833 --> 00:27:08,833
Okay, boss.

623
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:11,833
[DJANGO]
Hey, this looks delicious!

624
00:27:14,533 --> 00:27:16,233
Where are they going now?

625
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:19,167
<i>Let's cheer
Let's cheer</i>

626
00:27:19,300 --> 00:27:21,933
Let's cheer for the birthday boy
<i> Let's go</i>

627
00:27:22,067 --> 00:27:24,500
<i>Let's cheer
Let's cheer</i>

628
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:27,567
Let's cheer for the birthday boy

629
00:27:27,700 --> 00:27:30,167
<i>It's your birthday
But it's also mine</i>

630
00:27:30,267 --> 00:27:32,833
<i>I will invite
Everyone in line</i>

631
00:27:32,967 --> 00:27:35,233
<i>I will eat
A lot of orange</i>

632
00:27:35,367 --> 00:27:38,000
<i>While you need to eat
Only porridge</i>

633
00:27:38,133 --> 00:27:41,267
[LAUGHTER]

634
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:43,700
<i>Give us a big hand
And your hidden talents</i>

635
00:27:43,867 --> 00:27:45,600
<i>Men and women
Hold on to your balance</i>

636
00:27:45,733 --> 00:27:47,567
<i>All we wanna hear
Is the cheers getting louder</i>

637
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:49,367
<i>Take some meds
For that dancing fever</i>

638
00:27:49,567 --> 00:27:51,133
<i>And let loose
Let your body move</i>

639
00:27:51,267 --> 00:27:53,233
<i> Let's hear some joy</i>

640
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:54,900
<i>Give it up for Mister Rudy,
our birthday boy</i>

641
00:27:55,067 --> 00:27:55,633
<i> Let's go</i>

642
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:58,267
<i>Let's cheer
Let's cheer</i>

643
00:27:58,400 --> 00:28:01,267
Let's cheer for the birthday boy

644
00:28:01,400 --> 00:28:04,033
<i>Let's cheer
Let's cheer</i>

645
00:28:04,133 --> 00:28:06,367
Let's cheer for the birthday boy

646
00:28:06,467 --> 00:28:09,533
[ALL CHEER, CLAP]

647
00:28:10,400 --> 00:28:11,800
Gloria?

648
00:28:11,933 --> 00:28:13,033
Is it too loud?

649
00:28:13,133 --> 00:28:15,033
No, Pa, it's okay.

650
00:28:15,133 --> 00:28:17,233
It's so fun here.

651
00:28:17,400 --> 00:28:19,867
Does this always happen
when there's an occasion?

652
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:21,900
You should get used to this.

653
00:28:22,100 --> 00:28:24,900
That's how we celebrate
here in Ginintuang Lupa.

654
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:26,967
Whenever we get the chance
to get together,

655
00:28:27,100 --> 00:28:28,400
we do it.

656
00:28:28,800 --> 00:28:31,100
Besides, this doesn't happen
every day.

657
00:28:31,533 --> 00:28:33,400
Life is hard, you know.

658
00:28:33,500 --> 00:28:35,800
So, whenever we have time
to have some fun,

659
00:28:35,933 --> 00:28:38,400
- we make the most of it.
- [MAMENG] Mm-hmm.

660
00:28:38,500 --> 00:28:39,733
And you know, love,

661
00:28:39,867 --> 00:28:41,933
the people here
don't have much money.

662
00:28:42,533 --> 00:28:43,900
Some don't even have a job.

663
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:47,067
But what's important
is that we love each other

664
00:28:47,167 --> 00:28:48,500
and we've got
each other's backs.

665
00:28:48,633 --> 00:28:50,267
- [MAMENG] Mm-hmm.
- That's how we do it here.

666
00:28:50,433 --> 00:28:51,500
- [RUDY] Yeah.
- [MAMENG] Mm.

667
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:56,467
- [MAMENG CHUCKLES]
- [SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

668
00:28:56,633 --> 00:28:58,700
[SAM]
<i> They live so differently here.</i>

669
00:28:58,833 --> 00:29:00,833
<i>Back at home,
when there's an occasion,</i>

670
00:29:00,967 --> 00:29:03,100
<i>we get stressed out
just from planning it.</i>

671
00:29:03,233 --> 00:29:06,867
<i>But here, it's enough
that they can get together.</i>

672
00:29:07,567 --> 00:29:09,100
<i>No one needs
to prove their worth.</i>

673
00:29:11,167 --> 00:29:13,167
- [CHEERING]
- [STRUMMING GUITAR]

674
00:29:13,700 --> 00:29:16,367
[ELTON] I just want to tell you

675
00:29:17,067 --> 00:29:19,967
<i> That my mind is a mess</i>

676
00:29:20,967 --> 00:29:23,333
<i>I'm thinking
if I should follow her</i>

677
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:27,333
Because she captivated my heart

678
00:29:28,033 --> 00:29:31,500
<i> Do you know that I love you,</i>

679
00:29:31,700 --> 00:29:34,367
<i> And that my feelings are true?</i>

680
00:29:35,567 --> 00:29:41,467
<i>It's fine if I look stupid
As long as I'm with her</i>

681
00:29:41,567 --> 00:29:42,467
- [CHEERING]
- [CLAPPING]

682
00:29:42,600 --> 00:29:48,233
<i>Even if others say
That I'm getting crazier</i>

683
00:29:48,400 --> 00:29:51,700
<i>Even if someone dances
cha-cha with you</i>

684
00:29:51,833 --> 00:29:56,200
<i> Rumba or salsa</i>

685
00:29:56,900 --> 00:30:00,067
<i> Open up and let me in</i>

686
00:30:00,233 --> 00:30:01,167
[CLAPPING]

687
00:30:01,333 --> 00:30:04,300
<i>- I've got a flower for you
- [GABO CHUCKLING]</i>

688
00:30:04,433 --> 00:30:09,367
<i>What do you want me to do
to make you love me?</i>

689
00:30:09,467 --> 00:30:11,533
[CHEERING]

690
00:30:11,633 --> 00:30:15,400
<i> Open up and please let me in</i>

691
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:18,900
<i> I've got a chocolate for you</i>

692
00:30:19,067 --> 00:30:24,400
Give my heart a chance, my love

693
00:30:24,567 --> 00:30:26,900
- [CHEERING]
- [APPLAUDING]

694
00:30:27,067 --> 00:30:32,233
<i>Do you know nothing compares
To every moment I see you?</i>

695
00:30:33,233 --> 00:30:37,400
- But I still got a huge problem
- Yeah!

696
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:39,567
'Cause I'm still waiting on you

697
00:30:40,633 --> 00:30:47,233
<i>Even if others say
That I'm getting crazier</i>

698
00:30:48,233 --> 00:30:50,800
<i>Even if someone dances
cha-cha with you</i>

699
00:30:50,967 --> 00:30:55,567
<i> Rumba or salsa</i>

700
00:30:56,133 --> 00:30:59,233
<i> Open up and let me in</i>

701
00:30:59,333 --> 00:31:00,600
[CHEERING]

702
00:31:00,733 --> 00:31:03,567
<i> I've got a flower for you</i>

703
00:31:03,667 --> 00:31:09,433
<i>What do you want me to do
to make you love me?</i>

704
00:31:11,033 --> 00:31:14,467
<i> Open up and please let me in</i>

705
00:31:15,833 --> 00:31:18,767
<i> I've got a chocolate for you</i>

706
00:31:18,867 --> 00:31:24,467
Give my heart a chance, my love

707
00:31:24,633 --> 00:31:27,700
<i>Fifty kilos of gold bars
worth 400 million pesos.</i>

708
00:31:27,700 --> 00:31:29,733
<i>Transfer the gold
from your precinct</i>

709
00:31:29,867 --> 00:31:31,233
<i> to the NLEA safe house.</i>

710
00:31:31,367 --> 00:31:33,500
<i>If you put someone
in that kind of situation,</i>

711
00:31:33,667 --> 00:31:34,667
<i> they'll surely be tempted.</i>

712
00:31:34,833 --> 00:31:37,833
<i>For my wife, Gloria.
I love you.</i>

713
00:31:39,333 --> 00:31:40,767
<i>Gabo!
Django and his crew are coming!</i>

714
00:31:40,867 --> 00:31:45,233
<i>We're here to join the fun
at Rudy's birthday!</i>

715
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:46,500
<i> Who is Django?</i>

716
00:31:46,633 --> 00:31:48,433
He's the reason I was imprisoned
<i> for eight years.</i>

717
00:31:48,567 --> 00:31:50,533
<i> He's my mortal enemy.</i>
